{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumRowTangentBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumRowTangentBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumClosedForm"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.quad_max_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.quad_max_le","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L248-L253","doc":"`x C − x² L / 2 ≤ C² / (2L)` for `L > 0`: the quadratic in the number of rows above the\nstaircase is maximised at `x = C / L`.  Over `ℝ` because it needs the order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub_hminClosed_ge_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub_hminClosed_ge_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L236-L244","doc":"The same bound with the positive part made explicit: for `ℓ ≥ k`,\n`2 (Σ hook − hminClosed k r) ≥ (ℓ − k)² − r` with `ℓ − k` a natural number. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub_hminClosed_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub_hminClosed_ge","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L216-L234","doc":"**The energy of an `ℓ`-row shape is quadratic in `ℓ − k`.** If `2n = k(k+1) + 2r` then for every\ndiagram with `n` cells and `ℓ` rows,\n\n    2 (Σ_c hook(c) − hminClosed k r) ≥ (ℓ − k)² − r.\n\nNo hypothesis on `ℓ` versus `k`.  This is the inequality behind `REV_n = O(√n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hminClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.hminClosed","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L210-L214","doc":"The hook sum of the min-hook shape at `n = T_k + r`: `Σ_{i≤k} i² + r(k+1)`.  This is the\nclosed form `H_min(n)` of `hmin_closed_form_and_rev_sublinearity_probe.py`; that it is the\nminimum over all shapes is verified there and in `rev_sqrt_n_upper_bound_probe.py`, not here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_ge_tangent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_ge_tangent","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L175-L206","doc":"**Row-indexed tangent lower bound.** For every `j ≥ 0`,\n\n2 Σ_c hook(c) ≥ ℓ(ℓ+1) + (n − ℓ)(2j+1) − Σ_{i<ℓ} ((j − (i+1))₊)²,\n\nwith `ℓ = colLen 0` and `n = |μ|`.  Equality holds on the shapes `δ_j + 1^{ℓ−j}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L163-L171","doc":"For every `ℓ` the correction sum is at most `Σ_{d<j} d²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_eq_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_eq_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L157-L161","doc":"For `j ≤ ℓ` the correction sum is exactly `Σ_{d<j} d²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_Ico_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_Ico_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L147-L155","doc":"Beyond row `j` every correction term vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_range_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_trunc_sq_range_self","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L136-L145","doc":"The correction sum over exactly `j` rows is `Σ_{d<j} d²` (reflect `i ↦ j − 1 − i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.six_mul_sum_range_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.six_mul_sum_range_sq","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L123-L132","doc":"`6 Σ_{d<m} d² = m(m−1)(2m−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_range_succ_cast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_range_succ_cast","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L112-L121","doc":"`2 Σ_{i<ℓ} (i+1) = ℓ(ℓ+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.row_tangent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.row_tangent","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L89-L108","doc":"Per row: `L(L + 2i + 1) ≥ (2j+1)(L − 1) + 2(i+1) − ((j − (i+1))₊)²` for `L ≥ 1`.\nCase `i + 1 ≤ j`: the difference is `(L + i − j)²`.  Case `i + 1 > j`: it is\n`(L − 1)(L + 1 + 2(i − j))`, a product of non-negatives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_rowform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_rowform","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L68-L85","doc":"`2 Σ_c hook(c) = Σ_{i<ℓ} λ_i (λ_i + 2i + 1)`, rows 0-indexed, `ℓ = colLen 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.one_le_rowLen_of_lt_colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.one_le_rowLen_of_lt_colLen","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumRowTangentBound.lean#L59-L64","doc":"Every row index below the first column's length carries at least one cell. ","signatureChunk":0}]}